\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Compactness supplies regularity}
\date{2026-11-07}

\p{\ref{fdip-00EN} makes the resistance completion compact.
\citet{Corollary 6.4}{kigami2010resistance} then makes the
extended resistance form regular. On this compact space,
\citet{Definition 6.2}{kigami2010resistance} means that the
domain is dense in the supremum norm in the continuous real
functions. The corollary uses the form already constructed
and the compactness just proved. It selects no measure and
names no Laplacian.}
